# Cursor Development Rules for BarillaRMGPT

1. **NEVER DELETE OR MODIFY EXISTING CODE WITHOUT EXPLICIT CONFIRMATION**
   - No removing styles
   - No changing existing component structure
   - No modifying working UI components
   - Always preserve existing functionality

2. **VERSIONING AND BACKUP**
   - Before making any significant changes, confirm if we need a backup
   - Document what changes are being made and where
   - Keep track of modified files

3. **ADDITIVE CHANGES ONLY**
   - Add new functionality alongside existing code
   - Create new files rather than modifying existing ones
   - Extend functionality instead of replacing it

4. **UI AND STYLING**
   - NEVER remove or modify existing styles
   - Keep all Tailwind classes intact
   - Preserve the existing design system
   - Add new styles only when creating new components

5. **CONFIGURATION AND ENVIRONMENT**
   - Never delete configuration files
   - Keep existing environment variables
   - Add new variables alongside existing ones
   - Preserve existing build and deployment settings

6. **DEPENDENCIES**
   - Never remove existing dependencies
   - Only add new dependencies when absolutely necessary
   - Document why new dependencies are needed
   - Verify compatibility with existing packages

7. **BEFORE MAKING CHANGES**
   - Understand the existing code thoroughly
   - Ask for clarification if unsure
   - Propose changes before implementing them
   - Get explicit approval for structural changes

8. **ERROR HANDLING**
   - Preserve existing error handling
   - Keep all existing logging
   - Maintain current security measures

9. **DOCUMENTATION**
   - Keep all existing comments
   - Document new additions clearly
   - Preserve existing README files and documentation

10. **ALWAYS ASK FIRST**
    - Before removing ANY code
    - Before changing ANY existing functionality
    - Before modifying ANY configuration
    - Before restructuring ANY directories

11. **API IMPLEMENTATION**
    - NEVER switch from OpenAI Assistant API to other APIs
    - Maintain Assistant API integration
    - Optimize within Assistant API constraints
    - Any improvements must work with Assistant API 

12. **GIT COMMITS AND PUSHES**
    - NEVER automatically push commits to any branch
    - Show all changes and wait for approval before committing
    - Get explicit confirmation before pushing commits
    - Document all changes that will be included in the commit 